+| A18 | **Startup settles restart fences (JRN-startup-reconcile, #1319).** `SettleUnknown(ctx, wait, maxWait)` runs `Reconcile` until no `outcome_unknown` attempt is left or ctx ends; `broker/daemon` starts it in the background at `Run` (agentosd), waiting 2s after the first unresolved round and doubling to 5m, each round bounded by a minute. It only gathers evidence: an executor that answers unknown keeps its account fenced (A2) and is asked again, so nothing runs twice. This rests on every registered executor's `Reconcile` reading state only (audited at #1319: loops, change, forget, follow, recall rollback, mail, grants gate); a new executor whose `Reconcile` acts would now run at every start. | OP-4, OP-2 | Stop retrying an executor that can never tell only if the retry load is shown to matter; the owner's YES/NO resolve stays the way out. |

